Vendored BBRv3 backports (WildKernels, fatalcoder524) + sysctl prerequisites
(upstream Eric Dumazet) + 5.15 cwnd helper (WildKernels action-local).

LICENSE: these patch files are third-party diffs against GPL-2.0-only
kernel code (net/ipv4) and are distributed here under GPL-2.0-only terms,
NOT the builder's GPL-3.0-only license (see repo README License section).
They are applied verbatim to GPL-2.0 kernel trees at build time; no
relicensing takes place. Do not add SPDX headers inside the .patch files
(it would corrupt patch application).

Sources (fetched 2026-09-06, verbatim):
- 0001-net-tcp-backport-BBRv3-to-android{12-5.10,13-5.15,14-6.1,15-6.6}.patch
  + sysctl_*.patch ............ WildKernels/kernel_patches, common/bbrv3/
- 0001-net-tcp-backport-BBRv3-to-android14-5.15.patch
  + 0002-net-tcp-add-tcp_snd_cwnd-*.patch .. WildKernels/GKI_KernelSU_SUSFS,
  .github/actions/bbrv3/patches/ (no kernel_patches copy exists upstream)

Refresh procedure: re-fetch, diff against these copies, review the delta
for scope creep (new files outside net/ipv4, Kconfig default flips,
BBRv1 changes), then commit. setup-bbrv3.sh pins to these copies; upstream
movement never reaches builds unreviewed.

Vendored but unapplied on LTS-only trees (sublevels only grow):
- sysctl_*.patch (trees lacking proc_dou8vec_minmax; ours always carry it)
- 0002-net-tcp-add-tcp_snd_cwnd-*.patch (5.15 sublevel <= 43; ours >> 43).
  setup-bbrv3.sh applies only the 0001 backports; these stay on disk so
  the vendor set is complete.

